kunzite: Adreno 710 step 21, out of secure mode and a word written by the GPU (kgpu=21; the port map's 21).
21 continues gen7_rb_start after adreno_zap_shader_load, with the CP running from step 20 (WPTR =
RPTR = 10): CP_SET_SECURE_MODE 0 (cp_type7_packet 0x70e60001, payload 0) through the ring, as
kgsl does when the zap is loaded (it writes RBBM_SECVID_TRUST_CNTL directly only without one),
then adreno_spin_idle; RBBM_SECVID_TRUST_CNTL printed before and after. Then the port map's
proof: CP_MEM_WRITE (0x703d8003: lo, hi, value, as kgsl's gen7 ringbuffer uses it) of
0x6b677021 to GPU 0xe0008100 in the scratch page, followed by CP_WAIT_MEM_WRITES (0x70928000),
idle again, and the word read back from our side (cache invalidated first). A shared submit
helper appends to the ring at WPTR (no wrap), moves WPTR, waits for RPTR = WPTR and CX busy bit
23 clear for up to 2 s, and prints the CP/RBBM/context 0 status. Step 20 now records the ring's
WPTR, and step 19's blocks are found by a shared lookup of their undo entries. Nothing new to
undo: step 20's entry halts the CP first, and its registers go with GX in the slumber.

